steps.body:
A **subsequence** keeps some characters of a string, in order, and drops the rest: `one` is a subsequence of `stone`. The longest common subsequence (LCS) of two strings is the longest string that's a subsequence of both.

Two strings need a 2D table: `dp[i][j]` is the LCS length of the first `i` characters of `a` and the first `j` of `b`. Compare the last characters of those prefixes. If they match, that character can end the answer, so add 1 to `dp[i - 1][j - 1]`. If not, one of them is left out, so keep the better of dropping either.

```javascript
const a = "stone";
const b = "longest";
const n = a.length;
const m = b.length;
const dp = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => new Array(m + 1).fill(0));
for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
  for (let j = 1; j <= m; j++) {
    if (a[i - 1] === b[j - 1]) {
      dp[i][j] = dp[i - 1][j - 1] + 1;
    } else {
      dp[i][j] = Math.max(dp[i - 1][j], dp[i][j - 1]);
    }
  }
}
console.log(dp[n][m]); // 3, for "one"
```

`Array.from` calls its callback once per row, so every row is a new array. `new Array(n + 1).fill([])` puts one shared array in every slot instead, so writing one cell would change every row.

Row 0 and column 0 stand for the empty prefixes, which share nothing, so they stay 0 and the loops start at 1. Filling row by row means the cells above, to the left, and up-left are ready before you need them. There are (n + 1)(m + 1) cells and each takes constant work, so this is O(n * m) time and space.

example.code:
function lcsTable(a, b) {
  const n = a.length;
  const m = b.length;
  const dp = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => new Array(m + 1).fill(0));
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let j = 1; j <= m; j++) {
      if (a[i - 1] === b[j - 1]) {
        dp[i][j] = dp[i - 1][j - 1] + 1;
      } else {
        dp[i][j] = Math.max(dp[i - 1][j], dp[i][j - 1]);
      }
    }
  }
  return dp;
}

const a = "AGCAT";
const b = "GAC";
const dp = lcsTable(a, b);
console.log(`    ${[...b].join(" ")}`);
for (let i = 0; i <= a.length; i++) {
  const label = i > 0 ? a[i - 1] : " ";
  console.log(`${label} ${dp[i].join(" ")}`);
}
console.log(`Longest shared: ${dp[a.length][b.length]}`);

for (const [x, y] of [["GATTACA", "GCATGCT"], ["AAAA", "TTTT"]]) {
  console.log(`${x} and ${y}: ${lcsTable(x, y)[x.length][y.length]}`);
}

